# EN: THE RIVER PLATE QUESTION, third pass (22/9/2026, Juan: «try not to use only text»): the chart as
#     the header with the phase on it; one short line; the river drawn as two shores (flag; Buenos Aires's battery, Montevideo's supply)
#     and the passage between them (open/closed); Rosas's decree when his shore does not obey it; from
#     the split, the two leaders; the two clocks only while they run; the longer explanation behind
#     the arrow; the action. A port blockade is said on the shore's card (river audit 22/9).
# ES: LA CUESTION DEL PLATA, tercera pasada: la carta de encabezado con la fase encima; una linea
#     corta; el rio dibujado como dos orillas (bandera, bateria) y el paso entre ellas (abierto o
#     cerrado); el decreto de Rosas cuando su orilla no lo cumple; desde la particion, los dos lideres;
#     los dos relojes solo mientras corren; lo largo detras de la flechita; la accion. Un bloqueo de
#     puerto lo dice la tarjeta de la orilla.
#     Chart: "New Chart of the River Plate", E. & G. W. Blunt, New York 1840 (public domain, Gallica).
widget = {
 name = "gg_plata_header"
 size = { 520 252 }
 parentanchor = hcenter
 icon = {
  size = { 520 240 }
  position = { 0 6 }
  texture = "gfx/interface/gg_situations/plata_header.dds"
 }
  textbox = {
